# 1 Configure locals PostgreSQL 
> This guide is OS specific for Arch Linux, as this project is developed on this os
> It is perfectly possible to execute the same task on a different OS, but instructions will not be provided.
> These guide assumes you have an internet connection pacman and yay working and installed. 

### Tools and libraries
##### PostgreSQL
Java [arch wiki](https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/PostgreSQL)
This project uses PostgreSQL 18.4
1. install
    ```Bash
		sudo pacman -S postgresql
    ```
2. verfy the installation:
    ```Bash
		postgres --version
    ```
    output should look like:
    ```Bash
		$ postgres --version
		
		postgres (PostgreSQL) 18.4
    ``` 
3. initialize postgres
   ```Bash
		# 1. Create the directory as root
		sudo mkdir -p /var/lib/postgres
		
		# 2. Give ownership of the directory to the postgres user
		sudo chown -R postgres:postgres /var/lib/postgres
		
		# 3. Now, initialize the database again
		sudo -u postgres initdb -D /var/lib/postgres/data
   ```
4. start postgres:
   ```Bash
		sudo systemctl enable --now postgresql
   ```
5. open psql
   ```Bash
		sudo -i -u postgres psql
   ```
6. create your user and password
   ```Bash
		CREATE USER my_app_user WITH PASSWORD 'my_secure_password';
		CREATE DATABASE cloud_native_db OWNER my_app_user;
   ```
   and save these variables in a .env file (this must be gitignored)
   ```Bash
		POSTGRES_USER_NAME=my_app_user
		POSTGRES_USER_PASSWORD=my_secure_password
		POSTGRES_DB_NAME=cloud_native_db
   ```
7. update application.properties  
   add the following lines:
   ```Bash
		spring.datasource.url=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/${POSTGRES_DB_NAME:cloud_native_db}
		spring.datasource.username=${POSTGRES_USER_NAME}
		spring.datasource.password=${POSTGRES_USER_PASSWORD}
		spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=update
   ```
8. update dependencies to automatically read .env.
   refer to [paul shwarz official guide](https://github.com/paulschwarz/spring-dotenv)
   ```Bash
		<dependencyManagement>
		    <dependencies>
		        <dependency>
		            <groupId>me.paulschwarz</groupId>
		            <artifactId>spring-dotenv-bom</artifactId>
		            <version>$version</version>
		            <type>pom</type>
		            <scope>import</scope>
		        </dependency>
		    </dependencies>
		</dependencyManagement>
		
		<dependencies>
		    <dependency>
		        <groupId>me.paulschwarz</groupId>
		        <artifactId>springboot4-dotenv</artifactId>
		        <optional>true</optional>
		    </dependency>
		</dependencies>
   ```
9. start the application and check the HAL explorer
   ```Bash
		mvn clean spring-boot:run
   ```
   find the explorer at `localhost:8080`
